ENTRY            31875   20260608   20261124   20261124       3224
SUBENT        31875001   20260608   20261124   20261124       3224
BIB                 15         41
TITLE      Measurement of integral cross sections of some
            neutron induced reactions on rubidium at a TRIGA
            reactor: comparison with integrated data from
            evaluated data libraries
AUTHOR     (M.M.Uddin, M.S.Uddin, R.Khan, K.Naher, M.A.Shariff,
            S.M.Hossain, M.O.Rahman, M.S.Basunia, S.M.Qaim)
INSTITUTE  (3BANSAV,1USABRK,2GERJUL)
           (3BANBAN) Jahangirnagar University, Savar, Dhaka
REFERENCE  (J,RCA,113,437,2025)
           #doi:10.1515/ract-2025-0019
REL-REF    (O,31733001,M.S.Uddin+,J,RCA,101,613,2013)
           Previous measurements of the spectrum-averaged
            cross sections for the reactions 115In(n,n')115mIn and
            113In(n,n')113mIn.
FACILITY   (REAC,3BANSAV) 3MW TRIGA Mark II reactor
INC-SOURCE Dry central thimble (DCT) of the reactor
SAMPLE     High purity natRb2CO3 (purity 99%) target in powder
            form was pressed into two 10 mm diameter pellets
            (300 mg, 1.0 mm; 800 mg, 2.9 mm) under 10 tons and
            sealed in polyethylene bags. High-purity In, Ni, and
            Au foils (99.9% purity, Goodfellow) were cut into
            10 mm discs. The pellet was sandwiched between Ni and
            Au foils, used as fast and thermal neutron monitors,
            respectively.
DETECTOR   (HPGE) 20% relative efficiency, 1.9 keV resolution at
            1332.6 keV.
METHOD     (ACTIV) Irradiation time is 10 min.
MONITOR    (28-NI-58(N,P)27-CO-58,,SIG,,SPA)
DECAY-MON  (27-CO-58-G,70.86D,DG,810.7,0.9945)
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) Total uncertainty (7-10%)
           (ERR-S,1.2,7.) Counting statistics (1.2-7%)
           (ERR-1) Efficiency (4%)
           (ERR-2) Sample preparation (2%)
           (ERR-3,,0.3) Half-life of product (<0.3%)
           (ERR-4,0.6,3.0) Gamma-ray intensity (0.6-3.0)
           (ERR-5) Sample mass (0.01%)
           (MONIT-ERR) Monitor reaction cross section (6%)
STATUS     (APRVD) Approved by M.S.Uddin (2026-05-09)
           (TABLE,,M.M.Uddin+,J,RCA,113,437,2025) Table 2
           (SUPPL,31733014) Neutron spectrum
HISTORY    (20260608C) VT
ENDBIB              41
